{"type": "message", "id": "6002065f", "parentId": "18563399", "timestamp": "2026-04-04T09:03:26.842Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "functions.web_search:8", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"chordoma annual cases United States retinoblastoma annual cases US\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1001,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d78730c174684212\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: incidence and survival patterns in the United States, 1973-1995 - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"d78730c174684212\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/11227920/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c8ed6efbf2ed429\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis study provides new data regarding incidence and survival patterns of chordoma in the US. Additional epidemiologic studies are required to elucidate the genetic and environmental determinants underlying this rare, distinctive neoplasm.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c8ed6efbf2ed429\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"776e5e53cb97f013\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPrognostic Factors and Survival Outcome in Patients with Chordoma in the United States: A Population-Based Analysis - ScienceDirect\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"776e5e53cb97f013\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S1878875017306265\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b5646ee1e71c62d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma is a rare tumor that occurs along the axial spine in pediatrics and adults, with an incidence of <strong>approximately 350 cases per year</strong> in the United States. While typically described as slow-growing, many patients will eventually develop ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0b5646ee1e71c62d\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"April 27, 2017\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sciencedirect.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4b45cdf97055e621\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma: Current status, problems, and future directions - ScienceDirect\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4b45cdf97055e621\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S014702722100088X\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bffcecf5008c2eed\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nChordoma is an extremely rare cancer with an annual incidence of approximately 1 per 1,000,000 per year in the USA and Europe, leading to <strong>about 350 cases annually</strong>.1,2 The presumed cellular origin of chordoma is the residual embryonic notochord.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"bffcecf5008c2eed\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 1, 2021\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.sciencedirect.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c3d7c3e791ad7b2e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nDescriptive epidemiology of chordomas in the United States - PubMed\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c3d7c3e791ad7b2e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32342333/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b697eb8fc0a54530\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nResults: <strong>From 2004 to 2014, a total of 3670 chordomas were diagnosed in the US</strong>. The most common location was cranial (38.7%), followed by sacral (34.3%) and spinal (27.0%). The average age-adjusted incidence rate was 0.088 per 100,000 persons ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b697eb8